# text = Why do you think him mad My lord look at his dress , look at his eyes , look at his restless way , hear him cry " No Popery !" Mad , my lord So because one man dresses unlike another and happens to differ from other men in his carriage and manner , and to advocate a great cause which the corrupt and irreligious desert , he is to be accounted mad , is he Stark , staring , raving , roaring mad , my lord Do you say this to my face To any man , my lord , who asks me Mr Gashford , I find , was right I thought him prejudiced , though I ought to have known a man like him better than to have supposed it possible I shall never have Mr Gashford's good word , my lord and I don't covet it You are an ill-conditioned , most ungrateful fellow a spy , for anything I know .
